    "alternatePackage": {
      "@id": "https://api.nuget.org/v3/catalog0/data/2026.09.28.14.30.40/invarix.gate.agentframework.1.0.0-rc.3.json#deprecation/alternatePackage",
      "id": "Invarix.Gate.AgentFramework",
      "range": "[1.0.0-rc.4, )"
    },
    "message": "Superseded by 1.0.0-rc.4 of the Invarix.Gate packages. With another package lifting Microsoft.Extensions.AI.Abstractions (ModelContextProtocol, the OpenAI provider), Invarix.Gate.Extensions.AI 1.0.0-rc.1 to rc.3 can fail on the first request; rc.4 requires Microsoft.Extensions.AI 10.4.0. rc.3 and later also fix approval requests that could carry credentials unmasked (advisory INVARIX-2026-001, https://invarix.dk/security) and an Agent Framework defect that ended every run once an agent's total tool calls passed the per-run ceiling. rc.4 also reads dynamic SQL, always-true WHERE clauses and file tools with an operation argument.",
    "reasons": [
      "Other",
      "CriticalBugs"
    ]
  },
  "description": "Microsoft Agent Framework adapter for Invarix.Gate, the deterministic action firewall for AI agents on .NET. agent.AsBuilder().UseInvarixGate(gate).Build() routes the agent's tool calls through Gate's permission envelope before they execute, and at Build time reads the tools registered in the agent's ChatOptions and warns about any that cannot be intercepted, so a wiring mistake surfaces at startup instead of during an incident. Without an open GateRunScope, each run of the agent has its own run id, so per-run ceilings start fresh every run. Token accounting needs the chat boundary tapped, which Agent Framework's builder cannot install; for the most coverage, also build the agent on an IChatClient wrapped with UseInvarixGate from Invarix.Gate.Extensions.AI. Each tool call is then evaluated once, by that client, and another gated agent that this agent runs as a tool is judged under this agent's id and envelope unless the tool opens a GateRunScope for it. Observe mode is the default and blocks nothing.",
  "iconFile": "nuget-icon-128.png",
  "id": "Invarix.Gate.AgentFramework",
